# Speech models, if a machine has ever built the voice experiment.
#
# `experiment/voice` downloads a piper voice per language into here — 61 MB
# each — and coming back to main leaves them untracked and, without this line,
# unignored. That is the combination that reaches a commit by accident, and a
# model committed once is in the history for good. Ignored rather than merely
# deleted, because the size is the danger.
engine/voices/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Secrets — API keys live in the OS keyring, never on disk
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Business strategy and other non-public notes (PYSBG repo hygiene)
*.local.md

# Editors / OS
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Test artifacts
coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/

# Upstream anatomy source — fetched, never vendored.
#
# Startup.blend alone is ~293 MB, past GitHub's hard 100 MB per-file limit, and
# the push would be rejected outright. Both are downloads anyone can repeat from
# the Z-Anatomy project, and the README's asset-pipeline section says exactly
# where to put them. What this repository ships is the *output*: the .glb files
# in public/anatomy/ and the reports the manifest is built from.
tools/asset-pipeline/vendor/Z-Anatomy/
tools/asset-pipeline/vendor/Z-Anatomy.zip

# Coworker instructions for AI agents — kept local, not published.
AGENTS.md
